ts³11100669129³1version³13³1cache_oldmajor³18³1cache_oldauthor³18³1cache_diff_default_author³11³1revision³19³1text_default³1ip³2205.231.31.86³2ts³21100669129³2version³21³2name³2text_default³2data³2summary³3*³3text³3<b>[[Implementation Stategies]] Talk</b>

040119, JunkerIn:

Obviously a bare beginning. Please add, subtract, or whatever.

from intro page:

:"dedicated to the creation, in our lifetimes, of anarcho-capitalist societies around the world."

So this would seem to be where the rubber meets the road and maybe should be at 'Starting Points' along with "<nowiki>HowItWorks</nowiki>: how roads, schools, security, etc. work without a coercive state."

In any case, discussion or help is invited.

:BillStClair: I agree that [[Implementation Stategies]] belongs in the "Starting Points" on AnCapWiki, likely summarized as "How to get there from here". Note that we can begin creating anarcho-capitalist societies before the states have fallen in the geographic regions in which those societies exist. This is actually my preferred method. I believe that many of the world's governments will soon fall under their own weight, like the USSR. We need to be ready when they do with a viable alternative. Impatient though I am, I prefer that scenario to a shooting war.
----






